      en: "The Zharkent Mosque is located in the city of Zharkent, Almaty Region, near the border with China's Xinjiang Uyghur Autonomous Region. The city has a population of about 40,000. The mosque sits in the city center. The climate is continental, with cold winters. The building is a unique blend of Chinese and Islamic architecture, reflecting the cultural exchange along the Silk Road. It is a popular photo spot for tourists. The mosque underwent major restoration in 2005. The surrounding area has bazaars selling Uyghur crafts.",
